==Post-match==
Borussia Dortmund's manager Jürgen Klopp commented that the long season caught up with Dortmund. "It was late in the game and from the 75th minute it was very hard for us after a tough season, but we deserved to be in the final and we showed that tonight" he said.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.theguardian.com/football/2013/may/25/champions-league-final-quotes|title=Borussia Dortmund's Jürgen Klopp rues Bayern Munich's late winner|date=25 May 2013|work=Guardian UK|access-date=11 June 2013 }}</ref>
Borussia Dortmund defender Mats Hummels said the game was really close and very disappointing, and that they were the better team in the first 25 minutes but missed the goal that was needed.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/competitions/champions-league/10080988/Borussia-Dortmund-1-Bayern-Munich-2-match-report.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220112/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/competitions/champions-league/10080988/Borussia-Dortmund-1-Bayern-Munich-2-match-report.html |archive-date=12 January 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live|title=Borussia Dortmund 1 Bayern Munich 2: match report|date=26 May 2013|work=Daily Telegraph|access-date=11 June 2013 }}{{cbignore}}</ref>
Bayern Munich's manager Jupp Heynckes said that "We have achieved something unique".<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.theguardian.com/football/2013/may/26/bayern-munich-jupp-heynckes-borussia-dortmund|title=Bayern Munich's Jupp Heynckes: 'We have achieved something unique'|date=25 May 2013|work=Guardian UK|access-date=11 June 2013 }}</ref>

